# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Build outputs
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Without these rules a `git add -A` picks up the Gradle caches, the KSP-generated
# sources and a 20 MB APK that one command regenerates. Only the sources belong in
# the repository.
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
local.properties

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# IDE
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Signing material
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The keystore and its properties file live one level UP, outside this directory,
# so they cannot be committed even by accident — these rules are the second line of
# defence, not the first. `app/build.gradle.kts` reads
# `../photolog-keystore.properties` and falls back to an unsigned release build when
# it is absent, so a contributor without the secret can still build.
photolog-keystore.properties
keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Deliberately NOT ignored
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# `app/schemas/` holds the exported Room schema. It is generated, but committing it
# is what makes a schema change visible in review instead of only in a runtime crash
# on someone else's device.
